WEBVTT

00:08.234 --> 00:09.334
Diaho.

00:11.704 --> 00:15.644
It's been three years,
but you're still the same.

00:16.044 --> 00:20.414
Forty Days Earlier

00:21.184 --> 00:24.314
Jinto, your cat is in here.

00:24.524 --> 00:25.354
Sorry.

00:25.354 --> 00:27.484
Hope he hasn't given
you any trouble, Lafiel.

00:27.654 --> 00:30.524
Well, while we're on call,
we don't have much to do.

00:31.494 --> 00:34.124
But I don't know what to say
about your lack of sense.

00:34.394 --> 00:36.664
We're going into battle soon.

00:36.664 --> 00:39.654
Don't you think it's unfair
having him here?

00:40.704 --> 00:42.174
Don't worry.

00:42.434 --> 00:43.844
If we have to evacuate the ship...

00:43.844 --> 00:46.834
...I'll make sure to take
Diaho with me.

00:47.214 --> 00:49.274
I don't want you to jinx us.

00:49.274 --> 00:51.744
Anyway, that's not what I meant.

00:52.144 --> 00:54.384
There're no other cats
to play with here...

00:54.384 --> 00:56.114
...and no mice to catch.

00:56.114 --> 00:58.214
That's why I'm saying it's unfair.

00:59.154 --> 01:00.854
I have no choice.

01:00.854 --> 01:03.844
The Basroil's my home.

01:04.424 --> 01:07.264
You could've left him
with somebody else.

01:07.264 --> 01:09.524
There's no regulation against it.

01:09.734 --> 01:12.034
Common sense dictates
it's not a good idea.

01:12.034 --> 01:14.934
It distracts from the seriousness
of the mission.

01:14.934 --> 01:19.944
I heard the Abh used to go to
battle with children on board.

01:19.944 --> 01:22.244
It was hard to make a distinction...

01:22.244 --> 01:24.374
...between war and daily living
back then.

01:24.944 --> 01:27.214
But it's not like that anymore.

01:27.484 --> 01:28.514
Not yet.

01:28.514 --> 01:29.984
All right, then.

01:29.984 --> 01:32.754
When I get the chance,
I'll send Diaho to Lakfakalle.

01:32.754 --> 01:36.094
But I can't think of anywhere
to leave him.

01:36.094 --> 01:39.724
Everyone I knew from Officer
Training School is away fighting.

01:41.064 --> 01:43.294
If you want me to intervene
on your behalf...

01:43.294 --> 01:44.924
...why don't you just say so?

01:45.164 --> 01:46.534
Thanks!

01:46.534 --> 01:48.704
To be honest I was hoping
you'd say that.

01:48.704 --> 01:50.264
Come on, Diaho.

01:51.474 --> 01:53.994
The old lady doesn't
want you anymore.

01:55.244 --> 01:56.004
Idiot...

01:57.584 --> 01:59.674
It's been three years
since I've been back.

02:00.014 --> 02:02.104
Happy, Diaho?

02:03.114 --> 02:04.744
Three years ago...

02:06.754 --> 02:10.594
...I got the chance to see
Lafiel's home for the first time.

02:12.794 --> 02:15.894
The place where the stars meet...

02:15.894 --> 02:18.864
...was filled with glowing light.

02:21.104 --> 02:22.734
However...

02:22.904 --> 02:27.534
...the only light ahead of us
now was the light of battle...

02:28.214 --> 02:30.734
...and it was starting to
shine brighter and brighter.

02:40.824 --> 02:42.594
Imperial Calendar Year 955.

02:42.594 --> 02:45.564
The battleships of the
Star Forces...

02:45.564 --> 02:48.294
...had countered the advances
of the Triple Alliance...

02:48.294 --> 02:52.604
...which consisted of
the United Mankind...

02:52.604 --> 02:52.864
...the Republic of Greater Alcont...

02:52.864 --> 02:55.774
Imperial Capital Lakfakalle
...the Republic of Greater Alcont...

02:55.774 --> 02:56.904
Imperial Capital Lakfakalle
...and The People's Sovereign
Union of Planets.

02:56.904 --> 02:58.894
...and The People's Sovereign
Union of Planets.

02:59.104 --> 03:01.664
The counterattack had begun.

03:01.974 --> 03:02.744
As commander of the Third Fleet...

03:02.744 --> 03:04.044
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
As commander of the Third Fleet...

03:04.044 --> 03:09.184
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
...as well as overall
commander-in-chief...

03:09.184 --> 03:09.354
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

03:09.354 --> 03:10.054
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

03:10.054 --> 03:14.854
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

03:14.854 --> 03:16.294
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

03:16.294 --> 03:18.724
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
Additional forces of
training ships on standby...

03:18.724 --> 03:19.594
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

03:19.594 --> 03:19.824
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

03:19.824 --> 03:23.864
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

03:23.864 --> 03:24.564
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
Sparing nothing...

03:24.564 --> 03:24.804
Sparing nothing...

03:24.804 --> 03:25.234
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef

03:25.234 --> 03:28.634
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
...to reorganize the fleet
in terms of scale...

03:28.634 --> 03:29.674
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
...training, and top personnel,
the Star Forces have dubbed this...

03:29.674 --> 03:33.814
...training, and top personnel,
the Star Forces have dubbed this...

03:33.814 --> 03:36.644
Operation Phantom Flame.

03:37.414 --> 03:41.504
Now, the battle will truly begin.

03:49.454 --> 03:53.084
Operation Phantom Flame

03:58.734 --> 04:03.904
Banner of the Stars

05:18.684 --> 05:23.054
Month of Sesunaj, Day 5
Time 19:37

05:23.054 --> 05:27.354
Aptic System
Aptic III

05:54.884 --> 05:56.514
The enemy's command fortress...

05:56.514 --> 05:58.684
...will be within range
in 30 seconds!

05:58.984 --> 06:02.584
All ships to concentrate fire on
the second sector of enemy ships.

06:03.094 --> 06:04.754
All ships standing by!

06:05.264 --> 06:07.524
Target fire on the second sector
of enemy ships!

06:17.004 --> 06:18.474
Enemy escorts have
been destroyed!

06:18.474 --> 06:18.944
All ships!

06:18.944 --> 06:20.974
Prepare to fire the
electromagnetic cannon!

06:20.974 --> 06:23.614
Electromagnetic cannon
is ready to fire!

06:23.614 --> 06:24.544
Fire!

06:28.254 --> 06:30.054
We have been ordered
by the commander...

06:30.054 --> 06:32.224
...to retreat from the enemy's
mobile command fortress.

06:32.224 --> 06:34.684
Set the ship on a course of 150
degrees and follow the Lashkau.

06:51.274 --> 06:52.794
This is so tedious.

06:55.144 --> 06:57.844
If they knew they were
going to lose this badly...

06:57.844 --> 07:01.614
...they should've just run away
while they had the chance.

07:02.484 --> 07:04.954
Phantom Flame First Fleet
Command Ship Cruiser Lashkau
They must've miscalculated
our speed...

07:04.954 --> 07:06.314
Phantom Flame First Fleet
Command Ship Cruiser Lashkau
...Admiral Spoor.

07:07.094 --> 07:08.494
It looks as though...

07:08.494 --> 07:11.824
...most of the enemy managed
to escape before we arrived.

07:11.824 --> 07:14.194
They're probably waiting
for an opportunity to...

07:14.194 --> 07:17.664
Please stop telling me things
that I already know.

07:17.664 --> 07:21.034
If you carry on like this,
I'm going to die of boredom.

07:21.034 --> 07:22.404
Excuse me, Commander!

07:22.404 --> 07:25.774
The President of the Aptic System
would like to talk with you.

07:26.204 --> 07:30.004
Core Invasion Group
(Phantom Flame Third Fleet)

07:31.144 --> 07:31.814
Phantom Flame Third Fleet
Cruiser Sankau

07:31.814 --> 07:35.114
Phantom Flame Third Fleet
Cruiser Sankau
Message coming through from
Admiral Spoor of the First Fleet!

07:35.114 --> 07:36.084
Phantom Flame Third Fleet
Cruiser Sankau
Put her through.

07:38.484 --> 07:41.624
The First Fleet has demolished
the mobile command fortress...

07:41.624 --> 07:44.124
...of the United Mankind...

07:44.124 --> 07:46.094
...within the Aptic System.

07:46.524 --> 07:48.264
Full details are available...

07:48.264 --> 07:50.294
...in the report which will be
sent to you immediately.

07:50.294 --> 07:51.534
Good.

07:51.534 --> 07:54.604
Chief of Staff of the Phantom Flame
Third Fleet Space Navy Admiral Kenesh
As soon as a communication
link is established, send the file.

07:54.604 --> 07:56.534
Chief of Staff of the Phantom Flame
Third Fleet Space Navy Admiral Kenesh
I do not expect there to be
any changes to the plans...

07:56.534 --> 07:59.104
...but wait until you receive
confirmation before proceeding.

07:59.104 --> 07:59.834
Yes, ma'am!

08:00.974 --> 08:04.914
Looks like we came out of that
without much damage to the fleet.

08:06.644 --> 08:09.914
I presume we may now continue
with our plan to have...

08:09.914 --> 08:13.584
...Admiral Spoor's fleet
proceed to capture...

08:13.584 --> 08:16.084
...the enemy's gates starting with
Miskel, Dalmav and Demetel.

08:16.924 --> 08:20.094
The Third Fleet
and the Fifth Fleet...

08:20.094 --> 08:22.264
...will follow Admiral Spoor...

08:22.264 --> 08:24.264
...in order to set up
a main supply line.

08:24.264 --> 08:26.604
Meanwhile, the Second and
Fourth Fleets...

08:26.604 --> 08:28.574
...will advance from both sides...

08:28.934 --> 08:31.374
...and capture any inhabited
star systems...

08:31.374 --> 08:33.204
...in order to strengthen
our defensive line.

08:33.774 --> 08:35.974
It all comes down to
the speed at which we can...

08:35.974 --> 08:40.214
...cut through enemy territory and
reach our allies on the other side.

08:40.684 --> 08:44.324
We've received the report
from the communication ship.

08:44.324 --> 08:45.154
I'll put it up.

08:48.954 --> 08:51.794
How far can we advance...

08:52.864 --> 08:55.024
...before the enemy strikes back?

08:58.004 --> 08:59.564
I see.

08:59.564 --> 09:00.804
Recent events have made it clear
that our fleet isn't...

09:00.804 --> 09:02.204
I won't tolerate being a Duchess.
Recent events have made it clear
that our fleet isn't...

09:02.204 --> 09:04.574
I won't tolerate being a Duchess.
...powerful enough to challenge
your control of space.

09:04.574 --> 09:05.474
But tacky titles like Emperor are
best-suited to the Abriels.
However...

09:05.474 --> 09:06.704
But tacky titles like Emperor are
best-suited to the Abriels.
...I pledge that we shall resist
you ruthless invaders...

09:06.704 --> 09:07.374
...I pledge that we shall resist
you ruthless invaders...

09:07.374 --> 09:09.114
My name is Spoor!
...I pledge that we shall resist
you ruthless invaders...

09:09.114 --> 09:10.804
My name is Spoor!
...until you leave us alone!

09:11.214 --> 09:13.584
As a member of
the United Mankind...

09:13.584 --> 09:17.814
...I believe it is my duty
to undertake this challenge.

09:18.154 --> 09:21.624
We shall be happy to
honor that duty...

09:21.624 --> 09:25.064
...and we will certainly be
making that clear to you.

09:25.994 --> 09:27.764
I hope you do your best!

09:27.764 --> 09:28.994
Huh? What?

09:32.204 --> 09:34.964
Well, that was a boring speech.

09:35.474 --> 09:37.074
I feel bad for the President...

09:37.074 --> 09:39.374
...who speaks so passionately.

09:39.374 --> 09:40.504
Chief!

09:41.274 --> 09:44.044
While I was listening
to that fool drone on...

09:44.044 --> 09:45.774
...did anything happen that
I should know about?

09:46.314 --> 09:50.144
We have successfully secured
the space around Aptic III.

09:51.254 --> 09:53.184
We have seized 79%
of the enemy's...

09:53.184 --> 09:56.594
...anti-matter fuel production
facilities in the Aptic System.

09:56.594 --> 10:00.494
This means that our own
mobile anti-matter...

10:00.494 --> 10:03.324
...fuel production factories are
now 62% complete.

10:03.864 --> 10:05.704
Our plan to set up a base
on Aptic IV...

10:05.704 --> 10:08.174
...with a supply depot for solid
fuel and propellant extract...

10:08.174 --> 10:10.664
...is already 17% complete.

10:11.044 --> 10:15.274
Setting up the operations center
may take the longest...

10:15.274 --> 10:17.584
...but in approximately
218 hours, all of the...

10:17.584 --> 10:21.114
So basically, everything is
going according to plan?

10:21.114 --> 10:21.984
Uh, yes.

10:21.984 --> 10:23.584
So, next time...

10:23.584 --> 10:26.954
...just say there's no change
when there's no change.

10:27.594 --> 10:32.114
Don't you think it's about time
you learned to be more concise?

10:33.724 --> 10:36.394
Yes, of course. I understand.
I'll be more careful.

10:36.794 --> 10:39.424
Isn't this boring, Chief?

10:39.734 --> 10:43.724
What does the Admiral
want from me?

10:44.844 --> 10:46.344
Communications Chief!

10:46.344 --> 10:47.864
I want you to call Dikspa for me.

10:48.244 --> 10:48.834
Ma'am!

10:50.044 --> 10:50.944
Commander!

10:50.944 --> 10:53.114
How are the preparations
for departure going?

10:53.114 --> 10:54.944
Perfectly, Commander-in-Chief!

10:55.184 --> 10:57.284
Did you hear that?

10:57.284 --> 11:00.114
Now that was a
truly perfect response!

11:02.294 --> 11:04.024
Prepare to depart immediately!

11:04.424 --> 11:05.364
Yes!

11:05.364 --> 11:08.294
We'll send the Scout Ship
Squadron Dikspa...

11:08.294 --> 11:10.894
...to the Miskel System
for a reconnaissance mission.

11:17.504 --> 11:19.904
I am so bored.

11:22.114 --> 11:25.014
Inhabited Planet Lulukess

11:25.444 --> 11:28.844
Here's a toast to
my beloved blue Earth!

11:30.724 --> 11:33.514
Samson, you should have
gotten off the ship.

11:35.554 --> 11:37.254
There's no way I could do that.

11:37.254 --> 11:38.054
Why not?

11:39.124 --> 11:41.424
Officers get the cold shoulder
by the regular crew down there.

11:41.834 --> 11:44.834
They're there to have
a good time.

11:44.834 --> 11:48.134
They think we're going to
put a damper on things.

11:49.334 --> 11:52.104
I remember before I
became an officer...

11:52.104 --> 11:56.104
...I gave them a lot of grief
about intruding.

11:57.114 --> 12:00.014
I couldn't possibly spoil their fun,
now, could I?

12:01.914 --> 12:04.574
I guess that rules me out, then.

12:07.624 --> 12:10.124
Since you're nobility
as well as an officer...

12:10.124 --> 12:12.214
...you'd probably cause a great stir.

12:12.894 --> 12:14.594
But it's all an experience, right?

12:15.234 --> 12:17.694
If you really want to go down,
I won't stop you.

12:18.704 --> 12:20.534
Don't worry about it.

12:20.534 --> 12:23.974
I've had plenty of experiences
like that already.

12:24.744 --> 12:27.144
That's too bad.

12:27.614 --> 12:28.404
Yeah.

12:32.514 --> 12:34.484
But nature's great.

12:36.054 --> 12:38.954
You can drink up in a spaceship...

12:39.184 --> 12:41.784
...but you can't feel what it's like
to be surrounded by nature.

12:42.654 --> 12:45.324
Sometimes I regret
becoming an officer.

12:45.964 --> 12:48.994
The President of the Aptic System
wants to talk to us again?

12:48.994 --> 12:50.984
What does he want now?

12:51.234 --> 12:53.994
I've already heard him out.

12:54.204 --> 12:56.674
Maybe he isn't complaining.

12:56.674 --> 12:58.004
Then what is it?

12:58.544 --> 12:59.744
Well, never mind.

12:59.744 --> 13:02.434
You listen to what he says, Chief.

13:02.844 --> 13:05.544
Tell him I'm far too busy
right now.

13:07.914 --> 13:08.944
I understand.

13:10.184 --> 13:11.454
Transfer the call.

13:11.454 --> 13:12.424
It's coming through.

13:14.124 --> 13:15.624
Good day, Mr. President.

13:15.624 --> 13:17.324
Aptic System
President Makrit Talas
Unfortunately...

13:17.324 --> 13:19.264
Aptic System
President Makrit Talas
...the commander-in-chief
is currently occupied.

13:19.264 --> 13:21.164
Aptic System
President Makrit Talas
I will hear you out.

13:21.534 --> 13:22.664
What is your rank?

13:22.664 --> 13:25.634
I'm the chief of staff.
My name is Kufadis, sir.

13:25.634 --> 13:27.624
I see. Well, this is perfect then.

13:28.474 --> 13:31.574
Before I speak with your
commander-in-chief again...

13:31.574 --> 13:34.644
...there's something
I need to clarify.

13:34.644 --> 13:35.734
What is it?

13:36.344 --> 13:37.444
Well...

13:37.444 --> 13:42.154
...I think there's a fault with
your communication system.

13:42.154 --> 13:44.484
We're not aware of
any problem.

13:44.484 --> 13:45.544
That's hard to believe.

13:46.124 --> 13:50.394
I gave you a message that we
intend to fight to the bitter end.

13:50.394 --> 13:53.724
Yes. I do recall hearing
something like that.

13:54.134 --> 13:54.994
Well, then...

13:54.994 --> 13:57.604
...I wonder if it's our system
that isn't working properly.

13:57.604 --> 13:59.764
I could be wrong, but I'm positive...

13:59.764 --> 14:03.034
...I heard your
commander-in-chief encourage us.

14:03.604 --> 14:05.694
Yes, that is correct.

14:06.104 --> 14:06.664
Huh?

14:07.574 --> 14:10.544
I don't understand.

14:10.544 --> 14:13.284
I declare our intention to fight...

14:13.284 --> 14:17.384
...but the commander-in-chief
gives us words of encouragement?

14:17.384 --> 14:18.544
I see what you mean.

14:18.824 --> 14:21.654
In preparation for this
inevitable confrontation...

14:21.654 --> 14:25.824
...I did my best to cultivate an
understanding of Abh culture.

14:26.524 --> 14:28.694
But obviously it wasn't good enough.

14:29.564 --> 14:32.664
So, why did you become an Abh?

14:32.664 --> 14:34.974
An Abh? Me?

14:34.974 --> 14:36.594
You've got to be kidding.

14:36.874 --> 14:40.104
When I became an officer,
a warrior's title came with it...

14:40.104 --> 14:42.544
...and an Abh status
came along with that.

14:42.544 --> 14:45.684
I'll retire one day, go home,
and maybe take up farming.

14:45.684 --> 14:47.304
That's my dream.

14:48.654 --> 14:51.884
But why did you enter the
Star Forces in the first place?

14:52.324 --> 14:53.914
I was looking for excitement.

14:54.224 --> 14:56.454
When I was young, I couldn't
wait to go out into space.

14:56.854 --> 15:00.524
Once I got up here, I realized
it wasn't really what I wanted.

15:01.264 --> 15:04.734
But knowing how to
operate a spaceship...

15:04.734 --> 15:07.234
...isn't much use to you on a planet.

15:07.234 --> 15:07.864
Right?

15:09.234 --> 15:11.404
I figured if I became an officer...

15:11.404 --> 15:15.774
...I could save up enough money
to buy myself a little farm.

15:17.584 --> 15:20.684
Does that mean you're
going to retire soon?

15:20.684 --> 15:25.054
No. I figure I need a couple more
battles before I've had enough.

15:25.754 --> 15:28.124
I'll keep working until then.

15:28.324 --> 15:29.624
How did you figure that?

15:29.994 --> 15:31.524
It's a matter of feeling.

15:31.524 --> 15:34.894
It's my loyal blood that
runs in the family.

15:34.894 --> 15:38.764
I'm not sure what you know
about us, Mr. President...

15:38.764 --> 15:41.864
...but you will find a lot of variety
and differences among us.

15:42.274 --> 15:44.774
Most of us, myself included...

15:44.774 --> 15:47.774
...would not give our enemy
any kind of encouragement.

15:47.774 --> 15:49.214
In other words...

15:49.214 --> 15:51.544
...that commander-in-chief
of yours is...

15:51.544 --> 15:53.344
How shall I put this?

15:53.344 --> 15:56.044
Are you trying to tell me that
she's not normal?

15:57.114 --> 15:58.314
Choose your words carefully.

15:58.924 --> 16:00.414
Yes, I'm sorry.

16:00.924 --> 16:04.014
If you were in her place, what
would have been your response?

16:04.794 --> 16:08.834
I'd probably tell you
to do as you like.

16:08.834 --> 16:11.164
I'm afraid that's not good enough.

16:12.964 --> 16:16.564
Where did you say your
home planet was again, Samson?

16:18.544 --> 16:20.244
Midgrat.

16:20.244 --> 16:23.314
You probably know it by
its Abh name. Planet Dakufo?

16:23.314 --> 16:24.174
Heard of it?

16:24.174 --> 16:25.344
Sorry, no.

16:25.344 --> 16:26.614
That's disappointing.

16:26.614 --> 16:29.484
Not very well known,
but we do have a lot of history.

16:29.814 --> 16:33.184
We learned how to travel in
Plane Space before the Empire.

16:33.184 --> 16:34.654
Wow!

16:35.454 --> 16:36.924
In my grandfather's time...

16:36.924 --> 16:40.454
...our planet had to decide between
the United Mankind or the Abh.

16:41.134 --> 16:43.864
To cut a long story short,
we went with the Abh Empire.

16:44.864 --> 16:46.594
Why the Empire?

16:47.934 --> 16:49.574
If you must know...

16:49.574 --> 16:53.544
...our eating habits are quite unique.

16:53.544 --> 16:55.804
Outsiders are taken aback by it.

16:56.114 --> 16:57.644
Before we pledged allegiance...

16:57.644 --> 17:00.544
...the United Mankind
sent advisors...

17:00.544 --> 17:04.504
...who tried to get our leaders to
make us change our eating habits.

17:04.984 --> 17:08.024
When I think about it, that
was the reason for our choice.

17:08.024 --> 17:10.594
The Abh didn't say anything
about what we ate.

17:10.594 --> 17:12.524
Or at least not in front of us.

17:13.524 --> 17:16.494
We figured that if they didn't
care about our eating habits...

17:16.694 --> 17:20.194
...we could let them call Midgrat
by their name, "Dakufo"...

17:20.904 --> 17:23.164
...as a compromise.

17:23.374 --> 17:24.804
So what do you eat?

17:28.344 --> 17:29.534
Better not tell.

17:30.314 --> 17:32.914
I've lost too many friends
telling them that.

17:32.914 --> 17:35.674
But I'm not your friend.

17:36.284 --> 17:39.114
You Abh don't hold back,
do you?!

17:39.484 --> 17:42.824
You've known the Abh
way longer than me.

17:43.194 --> 17:46.064
It's only been three years for me.

17:46.064 --> 17:47.424
Did I insult you?

17:48.564 --> 17:49.224
Not at all.

17:50.394 --> 17:51.704
I see.

17:51.704 --> 17:54.334
The President wanted me
to reply...

17:54.334 --> 17:56.274
...with a demand for surrender?

17:56.274 --> 17:57.634
Is that right?

17:57.634 --> 17:58.734
Yes.

17:58.974 --> 18:02.174
Standing up and pledging to
fight to the end is an attractive...

18:02.174 --> 18:03.974
...election strategy.

18:04.744 --> 18:06.444
When I used the term
"ruthless invaders"...

18:06.444 --> 18:09.214
...I was just trying to appeal
to the voters.

18:09.214 --> 18:11.484
Nothing more than that.

18:11.884 --> 18:12.884
Also...

18:12.884 --> 18:14.924
...the President also asked
if you could...

18:14.924 --> 18:18.624
...spice up the demand with
racial slurs and such.

18:18.824 --> 18:22.494
Well, at least it's getting
more interesting.

18:22.834 --> 18:24.434
Too bad, though.

18:24.434 --> 18:28.034
He's got the order of
events wrong.

18:28.034 --> 18:31.344
I hate being taken for a fool.

18:31.344 --> 18:34.274
If he was clear about his
intentions in the first place...

18:34.274 --> 18:36.674
...I might've gone along with it.

18:37.614 --> 18:41.354
Besides, the commander-in-chief
will be here soon.

18:41.354 --> 18:44.724
I'll leave all that official
demand-for-surrender stuff to him.

18:44.724 --> 18:47.414
He just loves to
deal with those things.

18:48.454 --> 18:52.584
Did you hear what he told the
Hyde System when they gave in?

18:53.164 --> 18:55.154
No, I don't think I did.

18:55.434 --> 18:57.334
He was very impressive.

18:57.534 --> 19:00.804
Considering he's an Abriel,
it was high-handed, sarcastic...

19:00.804 --> 19:02.294
...and extremely effective.

19:03.134 --> 19:06.744
The task of governing
your world...

19:06.744 --> 19:10.734
...is not a priority for us.
In fact, it is far from elegant.

19:11.044 --> 19:12.284
If it were me...

19:12.284 --> 19:15.114
...I'm sure that I could have
put it much more elegantly.

19:15.784 --> 19:17.684
Oh, right. Chief?

19:17.684 --> 19:19.414
Yes? What is it?

19:19.624 --> 19:22.684
The President wants us to use
something called "racial slurs"?

19:23.724 --> 19:24.554
Yes.

19:24.764 --> 19:28.594
Yes, like, "you lousy
land-loving pig!"

19:28.594 --> 19:31.404
Or, "bunch of crawling
slack-jawed mud turtles!"

19:31.404 --> 19:33.304
"Land-loving pig"
and "mud turtle"?

19:35.574 --> 19:36.734
They're a little unrefined...

19:36.734 --> 19:38.864
...but there's something
refreshing about them.

19:39.344 --> 19:41.604
She's not seriously
thinking of that, is she?

19:45.514 --> 19:48.254
I'm not going to let you out,
Diaho.

19:48.254 --> 19:50.544
These squirrels aren't your prey.

19:54.524 --> 19:56.254
When I say "no," I mean "no"!

19:58.024 --> 20:00.124
You brought your cat?

20:00.124 --> 20:03.164
I couldn't leave him
onboard the Basroil.

20:03.164 --> 20:04.534
There's no one there.

20:04.834 --> 20:08.134
Did he enjoy his vacation?

20:08.134 --> 20:09.264
Probably.

20:09.634 --> 20:13.404
I took him to a place where there
were mice to chase and catch.

20:13.844 --> 20:14.704
Good.

20:14.944 --> 20:17.374
Yeah, but the captain told me...

20:17.374 --> 20:19.344
...I had to send him back
to Lakfakalle.

20:19.344 --> 20:20.644
She did?

20:21.184 --> 20:23.484
She thought bringing a cat
to battle...

20:23.484 --> 20:25.974
...was inappropriate.

20:26.284 --> 20:28.814
So, I've got to say
my good-byes here.

20:29.024 --> 20:30.044
It's too bad.

20:31.024 --> 20:33.824
I've started to like this cat.

20:33.824 --> 20:35.334
He's pretty cute, for a cat.

20:35.334 --> 20:38.234
Don't say things like that
in front of him.

20:38.764 --> 20:39.924
He'll get an attitude.

20:40.234 --> 20:42.534
I've never seen a cat
without an attitude.

20:42.974 --> 20:45.134
What a profound insight.

20:45.974 --> 20:47.164
Captain?!

20:48.844 --> 20:50.334
We've finally been assigned.

20:50.744 --> 20:52.644
We're with the
Battleship Squadron Latouche...

20:52.644 --> 20:56.374
...as part of the First Division
of the 1058th Battalion.

20:56.714 --> 20:58.704
We'll be leaving in twelve hours.

21:02.394 --> 21:04.084
This is sudden.

21:04.564 --> 21:05.724
I think so, too.

21:06.224 --> 21:08.424
But it's part of our training.

21:08.894 --> 21:09.954
What happens after this?

21:10.234 --> 21:12.254
We'll be heading to
a different system.

21:12.534 --> 21:13.464
Which one?

21:13.464 --> 21:15.524
They haven't given us
any information.

21:16.004 --> 21:19.834
We'll just have to wait until
we arrive to find out, Ekuryua.

21:22.414 --> 21:25.844
There's still two hours and eighteen
minutes of leave remaining.

21:26.584 --> 21:27.414
However...

21:27.414 --> 21:30.404
...I would like you to start
preparing immediately.

21:30.614 --> 21:32.724
Does anyone have a problem
with that?

21:32.724 --> 21:36.594
No. We were just killing time
here anyway.

21:36.594 --> 21:39.224
Very well. Officer Ekuryua...

21:39.224 --> 21:41.694
...get the Calike ready to transport
everyone back to the ship.

21:41.694 --> 21:43.594
We'll be heading back before you.

21:43.594 --> 21:44.294
Yes, ma'am.

21:44.294 --> 21:45.034
Let's go!

21:45.034 --> 21:45.554
Right!

21:47.634 --> 21:49.004
What have you there?

21:50.174 --> 21:52.574
I'm sure you recognize this cat.

21:52.774 --> 21:55.504
I thought I told you to
send him to Lakfakalle.

21:56.274 --> 21:58.414
I thought I still had time.

21:58.414 --> 22:00.384
I'll go and make the
arrangements now.

22:00.844 --> 22:01.954
There isn't enough time.

22:01.954 --> 22:03.954
You can bring him with you.

22:03.954 --> 22:06.624
But send him back
at the next opportunity.

22:06.624 --> 22:08.614
Yes. Of course.

22:09.154 --> 22:10.624
Oh, boy.

22:10.624 --> 22:13.824
You'd never believe she was
speaking to a fellow officer.

22:16.094 --> 22:17.084
Jinto!

22:17.464 --> 22:19.994
Do you know the name of
our new squadron commander?

22:20.264 --> 22:22.034
How would I know?

22:22.674 --> 22:24.844
Her name's
Hecto-Commander Atosuryua.

22:24.844 --> 22:26.564
Atosuryua?

22:26.804 --> 22:29.314
I think I've heard that name before.

22:29.314 --> 22:31.604
You sure are thick.

22:32.184 --> 22:34.704
Like frozen vegetables?

22:35.014 --> 22:37.954
She's the younger sister
of Baron Febdash.

22:41.924 --> 22:43.724
That was well done!

22:43.724 --> 22:45.984
Your Highness!

22:54.234 --> 22:58.534
kizukanaikoto ga
The things I did not notice

22:59.274 --> 23:03.334
konnani takusan aru
I didn't know there were so many

23:04.684 --> 23:08.274
kyoumade no jibun ga
I think of myself until today

23:09.554 --> 23:13.314
nasakenaku omoete
To be so pathetic

23:13.584 --> 23:15.724
kuyashii kurai
It's almost frustrating

23:15.724 --> 23:19.554
haritsumeta kimochiga
This tense feeling

23:20.824 --> 23:26.104
massugu ni muite ireba
As long as I keeping facing forward

23:26.104 --> 23:29.664
setsunasa no nukumori
This momentary warmth

23:30.034 --> 23:34.064
hajimete shitta
I understood it for the first time

23:34.604 --> 23:39.144
kimi ga iruto
When you are there

23:39.144 --> 23:46.384
itsumo pink no namida ga nagareteru
The pink tears are always flowing

23:46.384 --> 23:51.594
kono mune no naka wo afureteru
My heart is brimming with it

23:51.594 --> 24:00.024
kimi ga dokoni itemo dareto hanashitemo
Wherever you are and whoever you talk to

24:02.004 --> 24:07.144
issho ni itaiyo soba ni ite
I want to be with you, to be near you

24:07.144 --> 24:12.514
tsunaida te kara yubisaki kara
From our joined hands and our fingertips

24:12.514 --> 24:20.924
karadajuu no omoi binetsu tsutawatte
My body heat transmits the feelings inside

24:21.254 --> 24:25.624
tomerarenai
And I cannot stop it

24:31.564 --> 24:33.134
I'm recognizing again...

24:33.134 --> 24:36.304
...that your personality is
rather incorrigible.

24:36.304 --> 24:37.374
I see.

24:37.374 --> 24:40.704
Of course, I've had many
occasions to recognize this.

24:40.704 --> 24:43.514
And I'm sure there will be
many more.

24:43.514 --> 24:44.984
Hecto-Commander Atosuryua!

24:44.984 --> 24:47.614
This is a real battle!
It's not practice anymore!

24:47.614 --> 24:48.714
Ignite the main engines!

24:48.714 --> 24:50.614
It's going to be a race!

24:52.754 --> 24:54.984
We've received a request
from the Gamroil...

24:55.094 --> 24:56.454
...for space-time fusion.

24:56.454 --> 24:57.854
I salute your courage.

24:57.854 --> 25:00.954
Next episode...
Assault Ship Basroil
